{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197598",
      "title": "Understanding Screen Orientation Problems",
      "lectureOrder": 83,
      "videoOrder": 80,
      "sourceHash": "eceea88fb2caeade3d65e801ed548a27ea7d5719a6cf960b5443e681177417b4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "So that was the Dimensions API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 7.37,
          "en": "Very useful, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.37,
          "end": 9.8,
          "en": "Now, there's one thing we can't do with it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.8,
          "end": 12.62,
          "en": "and with our app at the moment, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.62,
          "end": 15.93,
          "en": "and that is rotate our screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.93,
          "end": 18.01,
          "en": "I mean, we can rotate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.01,
          "end": 19.52,
          "en": "Here I'm using a shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.52,
          "end": 21.44,
          "en": "but you can also do this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.28,
          "end": 24.94,
          "en": "with the menu on iOS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.94,
          "end": 27.08,
          "en": "and rotate your device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.08,
          "end": 30.213,
          "en": "And on Android, you can use these buttons to rotate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.12,
          "end": 34.49,
          "en": "But as you can tell, the screen doesn't adjust to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.49,
          "end": 35.763,
          "en": "It doesn't flip.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.73,
          "end": 39.3,
          "en": "The reason for that is that this app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.3,
          "end": 42.653,
          "en": "by default has the orientation locked to portrait.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.49,
          "end": 45.41,
          "en": "You can set this in app.json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.41,
          "end": 48.02,
          "en": "which is a conflict file picked up by Expo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.02,
          "end": 51.68,
          "en": "and this locks the orientation of the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.68,
          "end": 54.673,
          "en": "to a certain aspect, in this case to portrait.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.62,
          "end": 57.27,
          "en": "Now, this is maybe what you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.27,
          "end": 60.35,
          "en": "And to be honest for this kind of app, for this game,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.35,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "it would probably make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 64.483,
          "en": "to lock it to that orientation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.42,
          "end": 67.26,
          "en": "But of course you could also be building apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.26,
          "end": 69.53999999999999,
          "en": "where this is not locked in place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.53999999999999,
          "end": 72.5,
          "en": "and you can also unlock it with Expo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.5,
          "end": 76.18,
          "en": "by setting this to default, instead of portrait.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.18,
          "end": 78.65,
          "en": "As a side note, you can also set it to landscape",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.65,
          "end": 80.18,
          "en": "to lock it to that mode,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.18,
          "end": 82.75,
          "en": "but here I'll go to default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.75,
          "end": 85.21000000000001,
          "en": "Now it's not locked anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.21000000000001,
          "end": 88.23,
          "en": "And if we now flip this, it still doesn't adjust",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.23,
          "end": 90.73,
          "en": "because typically you need to restart your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.73,
          "end": 92.163,
          "en": "for this to have an effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93,
          "end": 96.174,
          "en": "Here I pressed R in the terminal to force a reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.174,
          "end": 99.753,
          "en": "and thereafter it's now flipping on iOS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.82,
          "end": 104.35,
          "en": "On Android, it might still not be adjusting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.35,
          "end": 107.15,
          "en": "For me it is, but it might not be adjusting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.15,
          "end": 109.807,
          "en": "In that case open this menu here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.807,
          "end": 113.113,
          "en": "and make sure that auto-rotate is on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.12,
          "end": 116.786,
          "en": "And once this is on, you should be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.786,
          "end": 120.573,
          "en": "to flip this screen on Android as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 123.93,
          "en": "Now, what you can see is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.93,
          "end": 126.131,
          "en": "if you do change the orientation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.131,
          "end": 129.2,
          "en": "the app might get broken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.2,
          "end": 132.42,
          "en": "Here on Android, we can barely use it still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 132.42,
          "end": 133.933,
          "en": "but it doesn't look good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.08,
          "end": 137.44,
          "en": "And here on iOS, it looks better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.44,
          "end": 139.37,
          "en": "but still not perfect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.37,
          "end": 141.6,
          "en": "There's too much space to the top now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.6,
          "end": 145.32999999999998,
          "en": "And if we open that keyboard on iOS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 145.32999999999998,
          "end": 146.77,
          "en": "and by default it's not open",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 146.77,
          "end": 148.82999999999998,
          "en": "because you can type with the keyboard,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 148.82999999999998,
          "end": 152.8,
          "en": "with your regular keyboard, into the simulator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 152.8,
          "end": 157.8,
          "en": "But if you do force that keyboard by going to IO, Keyboard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 158.344,
          "end": 162.626,
          "en": "and then you use that, you toggle that software keyboard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.626,
          "end": 165.06,
          "en": "then you see that that keyboard actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.06,
          "end": 168.23,
          "en": "overlaps the input and you can't actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.23,
          "end": 170.77,
          "en": "close it by tapping anywhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.77,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "So now the app is not usable anymore here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 175.98,
          "en": "I can only close it here in the simulator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 175.98,
          "end": 178.37,
          "en": "by using this toggle shortcut again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.37,
          "end": 181.493,
          "en": "But of course the real users of your app won't have that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 183.24,
          "end": 185.497,
          "en": "So therefore this is not working this well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.497,
          "end": 189.17,
          "en": "in different orientations, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189.17,
          "end": 191.47,
          "en": "And that is what we will work on next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 191.47,
          "end": 194.913,
          "en": "to improve this app for different orientations.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
